(D1 -- minimal repro. RESOLVED 2026-08-22: the manual previously said,
 at what was then lines 5013 through 5016 (that text is gone from the
 current manual, corrected in place), "It will not overwrite a .lib
 that already exists -- a repeat --shared build errors and asks you to
 remove the .lib first". It did not error; it silently rewrote the
 .lib, clobbering any hand edit. The manual was corrected in vox commit
 70ca1c2 to document exactly this behavior (LANGUAGE.md:5249-5252) --
 see the ledger's Discrepancies section, item 1. Needs --shared, so
 not auto-run; see shared/LIB-overwrite.vox for the fuller version.
 Re-ran 2026-08-22 against vox 0.4.9 (commit bb406de), from the repo root, in a scratch directory:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   V=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   $V docs/ledger/probes/libraries/D1.vox --shared -o d1.so
   $V docs/ledger/probes/libraries/D1.vox --shared -o d1.so
